# P14a-2 secrets manifest (operator-owned template; never put real secrets here)
#
# Format: name | file (relative to KIARABOT_SECRETS_DIR) | mode | consumers | rotation order
# The order column documents the manual rotation restart sequence after replacing a file:
# identity -> runtime/scheduler/model -> plugin-host -> adapter -> control -> panel.
# target-rotate-secret.sh validates the name exists in this manifest when it is configured
# via KIARABOT_SECRETS_MANIFEST, replaces the file atomically with mode 0600, keeps one
# timestamped local backup, and prints this restart order. KMS/hot rotation is deferred.
name|file|mode|consumers|restart_order
postgres-superuser|postgres-superuser.pass|0600|postgres|postgres
identity-migration|identity-migration.pass|0600|init-identity|identity
identity-runtime|identity-runtime.pass|0600|identity,identity-bootstrap|identity
runtime-migration|runtime-migration.pass|0600|init-runtime|runtime
runtime-runtime|runtime-runtime.pass|0600|runtime|runtime
scheduler-migration|scheduler-migration.pass|0600|init-scheduler|scheduler
scheduler-runtime|scheduler-runtime.pass|0600|scheduler|scheduler
model-migration|model-migration.pass|0600|init-model|model
model-runtime|model-runtime.pass|0600|model|model
admin|admin.pass|0600|identity-bootstrap|identity
identity-verification-key|delegation.pem|0600|identity,identity-bootstrap|identity
identity-token|token.hex|0600|identity,identity-bootstrap|identity
identity-request|request.hex|0600|identity,identity-bootstrap|identity
identity-receipt|receipt.hex|0600|identity,identity-bootstrap|identity
identity-signing-key|delegation.key|0600|identity,identity-bootstrap|identity
model-root-key|model-root-key.hex|0600|model|model
adapter-bootstrap|adapter.bootstrap|0600|adapter|adapter
onebot-access-token|onebot-access-token|0600|adapter|adapter
